{"path":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html","title":"Workspaces","description":"A workspace is a collection of one or more packages, called workspace members, that are managed together.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"workspaces","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspaces"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a collection of one or more packages, called "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace members"}]},{"type":"text","value":", that are managed together."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key points of workspaces are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common commands can run across all workspace members, like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo check --workspace"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"All packages share a common "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.lock"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file which resides in the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace root"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"All packages share a common "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/build-cache.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"output directory"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which defaults to a directory named "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"target"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace root"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sharing package metadata, like with "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-package-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.package"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/overriding-dependencies.html#the-patch-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[patch]"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/overriding-dependencies.html#the-replace-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[replace]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/profiles.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[profile.*]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" sections in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" are only recognized in the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root"}]},{"type":"text","value":" manifest, and ignored in member crates’ manifests."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" of a workspace supports the following sections:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-workspace-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Defines a workspace. "},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/resolver.html#resolver-versions","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"resolver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Sets the dependency resolver to use."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-members-and-exclude-fields","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"members"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Packages to include in the workspace."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-members-and-exclude-fields","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Packages to exclude from the workspace."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-default-members-field","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"default-members"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Packages to operate on when a specific package wasn’t selected."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-package-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Keys for inheriting in packages."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-dependencies-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"dependencies"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Keys for inheriting in package dependencies."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-lints-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"lints"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Keys for inheriting in package lints."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-metadata-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Extra settings for external tools."}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/overriding-dependencies.html#the-patch-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[patch]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Override dependencies."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/overriding-dependencies.html#the-replace-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[replace]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Override dependencies (deprecated)."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/profiles.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[profile]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Compiler settings and optimizations."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-workspace-section","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"},{"type":"text","value":" section"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To create a workspace, you add the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"},{"type":"text","value":" table to a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[workspace]\n# ..."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At minimum, a workspace has to have a member, either with a root package or as a virtual manifest."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"root-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Root package"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-workspace-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"},{"type":"text","value":" section"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is added to a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" that already defines a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[package]"},{"type":"text","value":", the package is the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the workspace. The "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace root"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the directory where the workspace’s "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" is located."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[workspace]\n\n[package]\nname = \"hello_world\" # the name of the package\nversion = \"0.1.0\"    # the current version, obeying semver"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"virtual-workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Virtual workspace"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" file can be created with a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"},{"type":"text","value":" section but without a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-package-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[package]"},{"type":"text","value":" section"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This is called a "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtual manifest"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This is typically useful when there isn’t a “primary” package, or you want to keep all the packages organized in separate directories."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/Cargo.toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"hello_world\"]\nresolver = \"3\""},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/hello_world/Cargo.toml\n[package]\nname = \"hello_world\" # the name of the package\nversion = \"0.1.0\"    # the current version, obeying semver\nedition = \"2024\"     # the edition, will have no effect on a resolver used in the workspace"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By having a workspace without a root package,"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/resolver.html#resolver-versions","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"resolver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" must be set explicitly in virtual workspaces as they have no "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-edition-field","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"package.edition"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to infer it from "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/resolver.html#resolver-versions","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolver version"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commands run in the workspace root will run against all workspace members by default, see "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-default-members-field","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"default-members"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-members-and-exclude-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"members"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"members"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" fields define which packages are members of the workspace:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[workspace]\nmembers = [\"member1\", \"path/to/member2\", \"crates/*\"]\nexclude = [\"crates/foo\", \"path/to/other\"]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/specifying-dependencies.html#specifying-path-dependencies","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" dependencies"}]},{"type":"text","value":" residing in the workspace directory automatically become members. Additional members can be listed with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"members"},{"type":"text","value":" key, which should be an array of strings containing directories with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"members"},{"type":"text","value":" list also supports "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.rs/glob/0.3.0/glob/struct.Pattern.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"globs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to match multiple paths, using typical filename glob patterns like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"*"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"?"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" key can be used to prevent paths from being included in a workspace. This can be useful if some path dependencies aren’t desired to be in the workspace at all, or using a glob pattern and you want to remove a directory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When inside a subdirectory within the workspace, Cargo will automatically search the parent directories for a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" file with a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[workspace]"},{"type":"text","value":" definition to determine which workspace to use. The "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-workspace-field","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"package.workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" manifest key can be used in member crates to point at a workspace’s root to override this automatic search. The manual setting can be useful if the member is not inside a subdirectory of the workspace root."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"package-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package selection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In a workspace, package-related Cargo commands like "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-build.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo build"}]},{"type":"text","value":" can use the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"-p"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--package"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" command-line flags to determine which packages to operate on. If neither of those flags are specified, Cargo will use the package in the current working directory. However, if the current directory is a workspace root, the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-default-members-field","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"default-members"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will be used."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-default-members-field","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"default-members"},{"type":"text","value":" field"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"default-members"},{"type":"text","value":" field specifies paths of "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#the-members-and-exclude-fields","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"members"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to operate on when in the workspace root and the package selection flags are not used:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[workspace]\nmembers = [\"path/to/member1\", \"path/to/member2\", \"path/to/member3/*\"]\ndefault-members = [\"path/to/member2\", \"path/to/member3/foo\"]"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: when a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#root-package","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"root package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is present, you can only operate on it using "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--package"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" flags."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When unspecified, the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#root-package","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"root package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will be used. In the case of a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/workspaces.html#virtual-workspace","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtual workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":", all members will be used (as if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" were specified on the command-line)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-package-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"package"},{"type":"text","value":" table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.package"},{"type":"text","value":" table is where you define keys that can be inherited by members of a workspace. These keys can be inherited by defining them in the member package with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"{key}.workspace = true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keys that are supported:"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[]},{"children":[]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"authors"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"categories"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"description"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"documentation"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"edition"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"homepage"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"include"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"keywords"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"license"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"license-file"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"publish"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"readme"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repository"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"rust-version"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"version"}]}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"license-file"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"readme"},{"type":"text","value":" are relative to the workspace root"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"include"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" are relative to your package root"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/Cargo.toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"bar\"]\n\n[workspace.package]\nversion = \"1.2.3\"\nauthors = [\"Nice Folks\"]\ndescription = \"A short description of my package\"\ndocumentation = \"https://example.com/bar\""},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/bar/Cargo.toml\n[package]\nname = \"bar\"\nversion.workspace = true\nauthors.workspace = true\ndescription.workspace = true\ndocumentation.workspace = true"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MSRV:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Requires 1.64+"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-dependencies-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"dependencies"},{"type":"text","value":" table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.dependencies"},{"type":"text","value":" table is where you define dependencies to be inherited by members of a workspace."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specifying a workspace dependency is similar to "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/specifying-dependencies.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"package dependencies"}]},{"type":"text","value":" except:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dependencies from this table cannot be declared as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"optional"}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/features.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"features"}]},{"type":"text","value":" declared in this table are additive with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"[dependencies]"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can then "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/specifying-dependencies.html#inheriting-a-dependency-from-a-workspace","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"inherit the workspace dependency as a package dependency"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/Cargo.toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"bar\"]\n\n[workspace.dependencies]\ncc = \"1.0.73\"\nrand = \"0.8.5\"\nregex = { version = \"1.6.0\", default-features = false, features = [\"std\"] }"},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/bar/Cargo.toml\n[package]\nname = \"bar\"\nversion = \"0.2.0\"\n\n[dependencies]\nregex = { workspace = true, features = [\"unicode\"] }\n\n[build-dependencies]\ncc.workspace = true\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nrand.workspace = true"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MSRV:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Requires 1.64+"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-lints-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"lints"},{"type":"text","value":" table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.lints"},{"type":"text","value":" table is where you define lint configuration to be inherited by members of a workspace."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specifying a workspace lint configuration is similar to "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-lints-section","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"package lints"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/Cargo.toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"crates/*\"]\n\n[workspace.lints.rust]\nunsafe_code = \"forbid\""},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# [PROJECT_DIR]/crates/bar/Cargo.toml\n[package]\nname = \"bar\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\n\n[lints]\nworkspace = true"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MSRV:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Respected as of 1.74"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-metadata-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" table is ignored by Cargo and will not be warned about. This section can be used for tools that would like to store workspace configuration in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":". For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[workspace]\nmembers = [\"member1\", \"member2\"]\n\n[workspace.metadata.webcontents]\nroot = \"path/to/webproject\"\ntool = [\"npm\", \"run\", \"build\"]\n# ..."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is a similar set of tables at the package level at "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-metadata-table","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"package.metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":". While cargo does not specify a format for the content of either of these tables, it is suggested that external tools may wish to use them in a consistent fashion, such as referring to the data in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace.metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" if data is missing from "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"package.metadata"},{"type":"text","value":", if that makes sense for the tool in question."}]}]}}
